Package: openaps-busybox
Version: __OPENAPS_VERSION__
Architecture: armv7ahf-vfp-neon
Maintainer: Bolke de Bruin <bdbruin@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends:
Replaces: ntpdate
Conflicts: ntpdate
Description: Static busybox providing the OpenAPS NTP client.
 A fully static (musl) busybox installed as /usr/local/bin/busybox-openaps. Its
 ntpd applet keeps the RTC-less ECU clock stepped and disciplined against the
 Debian NTP pool, run as a daemon from the shipped S56 boot script. Unlike the
 old ntpdate it links no OpenSSL, so it survives the stock firmware's move to
 OpenSSL 1.1. Replaces (and removes) the ntpdate package.
